# (draft riots); Miller Center; National Constitution Center; McPherson (1995); Berlin (1997); Foner's review of Bennett.
# Draft riots: Britannica lists 11-14 July 1863; NARA says only 'mid-July' and 'four days' and shows a telegram dated
# 13 July. No opened source gave 13-16 July, so the page gives NARA's wording and notes Britannica's dates.
# Left out as unverified: the 1861 income tax; the date of Butler's contraband decision; Sherman's entry into Atlanta
# on 2 September; Fort Wagner; the claim that Southern absence from Congress enabled the 1862 laws (US4.8 Q1 replaced);
# Psalm 19's Hebrew verse numbering; the citizenship clause of the Civil Rights Act (the DocsTeach transcript omits
# 'born'); the Miller Center's date for the Reconstruction Act (it says 8 March; Britannica's 2 March is used).
